------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the models are
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * detector.onnx: a card detector derived from YOLOX. It was fine-tuned, in two rounds, from the detector of
    the Kenbunshoku One Piece Card Game release B2.1
    (https://huggingface.co/JuicyKaraageNo1/kenbunshoku-onepiece, Apache-2.0), which was itself
    fine-tuned from the COCO-pretrained YOLOX-Nano weights published by Megvii
    (https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX, Apache-2.0).
  * recognizer.onnx: the cardvision recognizer (MobileNetV3-Small), trained to output one
    128-value vector per card picture. It was fine-tuned, in three rounds, from the Kenbunshoku release B2.1
    recognizer, which started from torchvision's ImageNet-pretrained weights (BSD-3-Clause code).
  * bank.json: one vector per known card, computed by the recognizer from card pictures. It
    does not contain the pictures.

Both models were trained with the open-source cardvision toolkit
(https://github.com/ryangswe/riftsight-vision) on labels made on frames of public videos, plus
synthetic composites made from official card art. No card art, video frame or label is included
here. PROVENANCE.md says more.

